  "worked_solution": "Substituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1+2} & ={a}_{1+1}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2+1 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=2$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2+2} & ={a}_{2+1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & ={a}_{3}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & =3+2 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=3$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3+2} & ={a}_{3+1}+{a}_{3} \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={a}_{4}+{a}_{3} \\\\ {a}_{5} & =5+3 \\\\ {a}_{5} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $8$ is the fifth number in the sequence.",
